<section class="content-section" id="runtime" aria-labelledby="runtime-heading">
  <div class="section-header" data-reveal>
    <p class="section-kicker">Runtime</p>
    <h2 id="runtime-heading">The local substrate underneath the Coven.</h2>
    <p>OpenCoven is not one app. It is the shared architecture for agents that remember, coordinate, use tools, and run inside boundaries builders can inspect.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid four">
    <div class="glass-card" data-reveal>
      <p class="card-kicker">/Coven</p>
      <h3>Project-scoped runtime</h3>
      <p>Launch and attach to agent work inside local repositories with visible output, history, and lifecycle control.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-card" data-reveal>
      <p class="card-kicker">/Harnesses</p>
      <h3>Pluggable harness adapters</h3>
      <p>Run Codex, Claude Code, and future agent CLIs through one neutral interface — project-scoped sessions, visible output, and lifecycle control without rewriting per-harness.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-card" data-reveal>
      <p class="card-kicker">/CastCodes</p>
      <h3>Terminal and code workspace</h3>
      <p>Keep the command surface local-first, open, and aligned with the agents working beside you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-card" data-reveal>
      <p class="card-kicker">/Next</p>
      <h3>Adapter-ready future</h3>
      <p>The system stays harness-neutral so new agent CLIs and client surfaces can join without rewriting the whole room.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
